WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Two people crossing the room. Each one gets its own ring.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
When they pass close together the system can mix them up. That is a real limit.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Three people. More bodies means more overlapping signal, and the estimates get rougher.

4
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.000
A weak, noisy signal with lost packets. Detection gets slower and less precise.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
An empty room. The right answer is nothing, and noise alone should not create a person.

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Only two sensors, so a single radio link. That cannot tell where anyone is.

7
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.000
So the system says it cannot locate anyone instead of guessing.

8
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Back to one person with the full set of sensors. All of this is simulated.
